        "original_id": "9e833064-9462-5542-9046-b0ef691beab5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rachel Jacobs\n- Companies: ApprenNet, Amtrak\n- Events: 2015 Philadelphia train derailment\n- Places: New York, Philadelphia, Port Richmond, Washington, D.C., Pennsylvania\n\nFacts:\n- Rachel Jacobs was born on October 3, 1975, and she was an American social entrepreneur and CEO of a tech company.\n- Rachel Jacobs had recently joined ApprenNet, an educational technology company, as CEO by May 2015.\n- On May 12, 2015, an Amtrak Northeast Regional train traveling from Washington, D.C., to New York City derailed on the Northeast Corridor in the Port Richmond neighborhood of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.\n- Rachel Jacobs was killed at age 39 in the 2015 Philadelphia train derailment while commuting between her home in New York and ApprenNet's offices in Philadelphia.",
